# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COLLEGE BOARD CONTENT — never commit any of this.
#
# The app ships no question content. Every user imports their own PDF exports
# from the official SAT Suite Question Bank. Nothing below belongs in git, and
# once something is committed it stays in the history forever even if you
# delete it later — so this file matters more than any other file here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The question bank, the extracted images, and the source PDFs
Cat Sat/database/
Cat Sat/images/
Cat Sat/pdfs/
database/
images/
pdfs/

# SQLite in every form it takes. NOTE: "*.db" alone does NOT cover the
# write-ahead log or shared-memory files, and those can hold real question
# data. This was a real gap in the first version of this file.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Any PDF anywhere — the Question Bank exports are PDFs
*.pdf

# Screenshots must come from the synthetic demo bank AND a synthetic profile.
# This whitelist once force-included two shots that had been captured on a
# machine with a real personal_plan.py, so they published a real exam schedule
# and target score straight into the README. shots.py now seeds its own throwaway
# profile; regenerate with:
#     python "Cat Sat/dev_tests/shots.py"
# and check the plan and calendar shots by eye before committing them.
Screenshots/*.png
!Screenshots/demo-*.png

# Test sandbox — rebuilt on every run, must never be committed.
dev_tests/_sandbox/
**/dev_tests/_sandbox/
dev_tests/shots/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Normal ignores
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
Cat Sat/dev_tests/_sandbox/
Cat Sat/dev_tests/shots/

.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Your own profile — scores, test dates, name. Never commit this.
Cat Sat/database/profile.json
database/profile.json
profile.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PERSONAL DATA — never commit any of this.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A hand-written plan and a profile both contain one real student's test
# scores, weaknesses and schedule. They are also wrong for anybody else: the
# app generates a plan from each user's own score report instead.
Cat Sat/personal_plan.py
personal_plan.py
Cat Sat/database/profile.json
database/profile.json
profile.json

# The development changelog is written to one person, in the second person.
Cat Sat/UPGRADES.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# App builds
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PyInstaller output. GitHub Actions rebuilds these on every tag; committing
# a 100 MB binary to the repo is how a project ends up too big to clone.
dist/
build/*.toc
build/*.pkg
build/CatPrep/
*.spec.bak
"CatPrep Data"/
CatPrep Data/

# PyInstaller's working folder. `python -m PyInstaller build/catprep.spec` does
# its intermediate work in build/<spec name>/, right next to the spec, and that
# is hundreds of files that must never be committed. dist/ is ignored above.
build/catprep/
